        "original_id": "4e65c01f-8611-52c2-a5dd-1c871516c6c7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Fincke, Scott Kelly, Gennady Padalka, André Kuipers\n- Roles: astronauts, International Space Station commanders\n- Organizations: International Space Station\n- Projects: Expeditions 26, 45, 46, Soyuz TMA-4\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Fincke was born on March 14, 1967, and is an American astronaut.\n- Soyuz TMA-4 flew Gennady Padalka of Russia, Michael Fincke of the United States, and André Kuipers of the Netherlands to the International Space Station.\n- Scott Kelly was a veteran of four space flights and commanded the International Space Station on Expeditions 26, 45, and 46.\n- Michael Fincke formerly held the American record for the most time in space with 381.6 days.\n- Scott Kelly broke Michael Fincke's American record for the most time in space on October 16, 2015.",
